<%= essentials_form_for @kit, remote: request.xhr?, data: {controller: "form-input duplicate-items"} do |f| %>
  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6">
    <%= essentials_error_summary(@kit) %>

    <%#
      Above the form, not below it. This warns about something that cannot be undone -- and it sat
      under both cards, measured at **y=922 on a 720px viewport**, 765px below the `h1`. You had to
      scroll past the thing you were composing to be told composing it was final.

      A callout that qualifies the *whole task* belongs directly under the page header. One that
      qualifies a single section sits with that section -- which is why the two reminder callouts on
      the partner forms stay where they are, next to the fields they describe. See design.md.

      "via the kit's item" was the wording, and it leaked an implementation detail: a kit *is* an
      item by STI, which is true and not something a user knows. It names the screen instead.
    %>
    <%= render "shared/essentials/callout", tone: :warning, role: "status" do %>
      <p class="font-semibold">The items in a kit are fixed once you save.</p>
      <p class="mt-1">
        Get the contents right before saving — they cannot be changed afterwards. The name, value
        and partner visibility can be edited later from
        <%= link_to "Items &amp; inventory".html_safe, items_path, class: "font-medium underline" %>.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%= render "shared/essentials/card", title: "Kit details" do %>
      <%= f.input :name, label: "Name" %>
      <%= f.input :visible_to_partners, label: "Kit is visible to partners?", as: :boolean %>
      <%= f.input :value_in_dollars, label: "Value for kit", input_html: {min: 0} %>
    <% end %>

    <%# The kit's own builder, not `fields_for @kit.kit_item`: main made Kit an STI subclass of
        Item, so a kit *is* the item and its line items hang off it directly. There is no nested
        record left to open a scope for. %>
    <%= render "shared/essentials/card", title: "Items in this kit", padded: false do %>
      <%= render "line_items/line_item_table", form: f, id: "kit_line_items", noun: "kit" %>
    <% end %>

    <%= essentials_form_actions do %>
      <%= f.button :button, "Save", class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :primary, size: :md),
            data: {disable_with: "Saving...", "duplicate-items-target": "itemSubmitButton"} %>
      <%= essentials_link_button "Cancel", kits_path, variant: :ghost, size: :md %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
